praxis_lock
===========

This directory is a Python transcription, at toy parameters, of the witness
encryption scheme defined in:

  praxis-lean: Lean 4 proofs for Praxis
  David Tse, Nikhil Vanjani, Psi Vesely
  https://github.com/psivesely/praxis-lean   (Apache License 2.0)

which formalises the scheme of the paper

  Praxis: Practical Witness Encryption for NP
  David Tse, Nikhil Vanjani, Psi Vesely
  Cryptology ePrint Archive, Paper 2026/2971   (CC BY 4.0)

The scheme, its parameters and its proofs are the work of those authors. The
definitions followed here are in Praxis/Enc.lean, Praxis/Dec.lean,
Praxis/QAP.lean, Praxis/Domain.lean, Praxis/Grid.lean, Praxis/Kummer.lean,
Praxis/Forms.lean, Praxis/Stack.lean, Praxis/Search.lean, Praxis/Keys.lean,
Praxis/Published.lean, Praxis/Params.lean and Praxis/Constants.lean of that
repository, at commit 60d3def.

This transcription is independent work. It is not affiliated with or endorsed
by the authors, and any errors in it are not theirs. Because it is derived from
an Apache-2.0 work, this directory is distributed under the Apache License 2.0
(see LICENSE in this directory); the rest of the repository is MIT.

The subdirectory `encoding/` (statements about BN254 arithmetic and a Groth16
verifier written as gates) is not derived from the Lean development or from the
paper's construction. It is original to this project, written from first
principles, and is distributed under the same Apache License 2.0.

Changes from the original: rewritten in Python; the honest quotient polynomials,
which the Lean text obtains by an existence argument, are computed explicitly;
decryption collapses the sums of `evalComb` using the rank-one shape of the
honest stack; the random oracles are instantiated with SHA-2; evaluation points
are derived by hashing the parameters; a baby-step giant-step search replaces
the linear scan of `findT`.
